<title>USA: S&amp;P issues credit reports for 23 utilities.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P issues credit reports for 23 utilities.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Sept 23  - Standard &amp; Poor's Corporate Utilities Ratings Group has issued detailed 12-16 page credit reports on the utilities listed below. These reports are available to subscribers through Standard &amp; Poor's Utilities Rating Service, which covers 250 investor-owned electric, gas, water, and telecommunications companies in the U.S. The reports published this month are as follows:</p>
<p>-- Alabama Gas Corp.</p>
<p>-- Alabama Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Appalachian Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Atlantic City Electric Co.</p>
<p>-- Baton Rouge Water Works Co.</p>
<p>-- Central Hudson Gas &amp; Electric Corp.</p>
<p>-- Columbus Southern Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Energen Corp.</p>
<p>-- Enogex Inc.</p>
<p>-- Georgia Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Gulf Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Indiana Michigan Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Kentucky Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Mississippi Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Monongahela Power Co.</p>
<p>-- National Fuel Gas Co.</p>
<p>-- Ohio Power Co.</p>
<p>-- PG Energy Inc.</p>
<p>-- Potomac Edison Co.</p>
<p>-- Primergy</p>
<p>-- Savannah Electric &amp; Power Co.</p>
<p>-- Tucson Electric Power Co.</p>
<p>-- West Penn Power Co.</p>
<p>For more information about the Utilities Rating Service or to obtain a complimentary report on one of the utilities listed above, please call (212) 208-8830.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
